}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Satori Hikami & Cat CC''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Hikami is an interesting cat, as she has the ability to knockback [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] enemies, albeit at a small 30% chance. Her recharge rate is decent, as she can be spammed at an interval of about ten seconds. However, her range is abysmal, meaning almost all enemies within [[Legend Stages|Stories of Legend]] subchapters and [[Special Events|Event Stages]] will eliminate her quickly.

With proper meatshielding from cats like [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Cat]], [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Cat]], [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Wall Cat]], and [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Wall Cat]], she might be able to get some hits in before she dies, although that is the only thing she will do.

Otherwise, because of her low range, she is not ideal for use in most stages as an attacker, so it is best to use others like [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Salon Cat]] or [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]].

Keep in mind that if you are thinking of using her purely for niche, there is a much better readily available cat: [[Pirate Cat (Rare Cat)|Dread Pirate Cately]], or Pirate Cat. Catley has a greater chance to knockback dangerous enemies like [[Bore]] and [[Berserkory]], and [[Talents]] making him readily useable and more flexible than this cat. Additionally, Catley has more range than Satori.

